insert into public.announcements ("id","slug","title","audience","created_at","author","image","link","body") values
('news-10th-report','10th-sata-annual-scientific-conference','10th SATA Annual Scientific Conference','all','2026-06-05T09:00:00.000Z','SATA Secretariat','/images/news/conference-2026-report.jpg','{"label":"Conference photos","url":"https://photos.app.goo.gl/jVnPy6an2cgKBMRs5"}'::jsonb,'**Theme:** Beyond the Operating Room: The Role of the Anaesthesiologist in Critical Care

**Dates & venue:** 20th – 22nd May 2026, City Garden Park Hall, Mbeya

## Executive summary

The 10th Annual Scientific Conference is a flagship event for the Society of Anaesthesiologists of Tanzania (SATA). It provides a dedicated forum for anaesthesiologists and critical care professionals to convene, discuss the selected theme, and advance the specialty. The conference featured scientific sessions, abstract presentations, plenary discussions, and practical workshops.

The conference hosted approximately 200 delegates from across Tanzania, 12 exhibitors, 4 pre-conference workshops, and 10 scientific abstracts. The event was highly appreciated by participants for significantly increasing clinical knowledge, strengthening professional networks, and developing soft skills. Importantly, the conference addressed under-discussed topics in critical care and charted a clear way forward for advancing anaesthesia and intensive care services in Tanzania.

## Background

SATA is a non-governmental professional association of physician anaesthesiologists and non-physician anaesthesia providers. Its core mission is to advance anaesthesia and critical care services in Tanzania through education, advocacy, and research.

The Annual Scientific Conference is SATA''s primary academic event. It brings together physicians, non-physician anaesthetists, residents, and trainees to discuss a selected theme, update knowledge on current international guidelines, and present scientific abstracts. This platform is vital for capacity building, especially for younger researchers and providers working in district and regional hospitals where most anaesthesia in Tanzania is delivered.

## Scientific programme

Keynote lectures and plenary sessions were led by national and international experts. Topics covered included:

1. Advanced anaesthesia techniques and perioperative medicine
2. Critical care management and ICU best practices
3. Healthcare systems strengthening for surgical and critical care in low-resource settings

## Pre-conference workshops

Hands-on workshops were conducted before the main conference to build practical skills:

- Mechanical Ventilation: hands-on training to improve ICU and operating theatre management of ventilated patients.
- Point of Care Ultrasound (POCUS): skills for rapid bedside diagnosis and safer procedural guidance.
- Advanced Cardiac Life Support (ACLS): life-saving emergency response skills for cardiac arrest management.

## Research presentations

Research remained a cornerstone of the conference. Ten abstracts were presented through oral and poster sessions, showcasing locally relevant research, innovative approaches to patient care in resource-limited settings, and emerging evidence to inform future clinical practice, education, and policy.

## Awards & recognition

**Best Abstract Presentation: Dr Hassan Vuai.** SATA extends sincere gratitude to the faculty, organising committee, sponsors, exhibitors, and partners whose support contributed to the success of the conference.

## Recommendations

1. Expand skills workshops: roll out mechanical ventilation, POCUS, and ACLS training to our zones to build capacity where it is most needed.
2. Advocate for essential equipment: pulse oximeters, ventilators, and other critical care equipment in CEmONC centres and ICUs.
3. Strengthen partnerships with the Ministry of Health, WFSA, WHO, and other partners to align with the National Surgical, Obstetric and Anaesthesia Plan (NSOAP).
4. Keep prioritising critical care, perioperative medicine, and patient safety in future conferences and CME programmes.'),
('news-10th-announcement','10th-sata-scientific-conference-agm-mbeya-may-2026','10th SATA Scientific Conference & Annual General Meeting, Mbeya, May 2026','all','2026-02-04T09:00:00.000Z','SATA Secretariat','/images/news/conference-2026-announcement.png','{"label":"Submit an abstract","url":"https://forms.gle/kxzoDjiKTsH63ejE8"}'::jsonb,'SATA announced the 10th Scientific Conference and Annual General Meeting (AGM), **20th – 22nd May 2026** at City Park Garden, Mbeya. The milestone conference brought together anaesthesiologists, residents, registrars, nurse anaesthetists, and international delegates to advance scientific knowledge, clinical skills, and professional collaboration.

**Theme:** "Beyond the Operating Room: Expanding the Horizon of Anaesthesiologists in Critical Care"

## Scientific programme

- Scientific oral and poster presentations
- Evidence-based plenary lectures and panel discussions
- Hands-on skills workshops
- Updates on best practices in anaesthesia and critical care
- The SATA Annual General Meeting (AGM)

## Registration fees (TZS)

- SATA Member: 150,000
- Non-SATA Member: 250,000
- Other Specialities: 150,000
- Non Physicians: 150,000
- Residents: 100,000
- Non Physician Trainees: 100,000
- International Delegates: 250,000
- Workshops: 60,000

## Workshops

Interactive, hands-on workshops enhanced practical skills in critical care and perioperative medicine. Each workshop was limited to 30 participants, allocated first-come, first-served.

1. ICU Ultrasound Uncovered: See What Matters
2. Ventilator Secrets: From Basic to Mastery
3. Decoding the Critical Brain: Neuromonitoring Workshop
4. Back to the Beat: ACLS Refresher
5. Investigate to Innovate: ICU Research Paths

## Sponsorship packages

- Diamond Sponsor: TZS 20,000,000. Opening and closing ceremony recognition, one general session, premium exhibit space, four complimentary registrations, conference bag sponsorship, logo on the registration page and SATA website.
- Platinum Sponsor: TZS 15,000,000. Sponsorship of one general session, two exhibit spaces, three complimentary registrations, logo in the e-brochure and on the SATA website.
- Gold Sponsor: TZS 10,000,000. Sponsorship of one workshop or hot-topics session, one exhibit space, two complimentary registrations.
- Silver Sponsor: TZS 5,000,000. Sponsorship of one breakout session, one complimentary registration, one-year listing on the SATA website.

## Call for abstracts

Abstracts of 300 words or less were invited on innovation and best practice, perioperative patient safety, regional anaesthesia and pain management, critical care and emergency response, surgical safety, anaesthesia in resource-limited settings, monitoring and medication safety, maternal and obstetric anaesthesia, paediatric and neonatal care, simulation and education, and health-system strengthening. All submissions underwent peer review. Submission deadline: 30 April 2026.'),
('news-masterclass','master-class-course-in-anesthesia','Master Class Course in Anaesthesia','all','2025-07-24T09:00:00.000Z','SATA Secretariat','/images/news/masterclass-2025.jpg','{"label":"Workshop pictures","url":"https://drive.google.com/drive/mobile/folders/1Fl-YX0WOZPw33UlLZWyzyDFv8GBIdOQ9"}'::jsonb,'**Organised by:** Society of Anaesthesiologists of Tanzania (SATA) and AAFRIN Medihealth Solutions Ltd, in collaboration with the Anesthesia Patient Safety Foundation (APSF).

**Date:** 22nd to 23rd July 2025 · **Location:** MUHAS MOI and MNH, Tanzania

## Overview

SATA and AAFRIN Medihealth Solutions Ltd, in collaboration with APSF, successfully hosted a master class course in anaesthesia in Tanzania. The event brought together renowned experts from India and local practitioners to share knowledge and advances in the field.

## Highlights

- Twelve experts from India shared their expertise in regional anaesthesia, POCUS, high-risk obstetrics, paediatric anaesthesia, and cardiac anaesthesia.
- The course focused on problem-based learning, hands-on training, and scenario-based discussions to strengthen clinical decision-making.
- Participants took part in master classes, didactic lectures, and group-based hands-on training.

## Key takeaways

- The latest advances and innovations in anaesthesia were showcased.
- The event provided a platform for knowledge exchange, collaboration, and inspiration among practitioners.
- Participants gained hands-on experience in a range of anaesthesia techniques and procedures.

## Recommendations

- Future events should continue to focus on practical training and problem-based learning.
- Provide more opportunities for networking and collaboration among practitioners.

The master class was a resounding success and a reminder of the importance of continuous education and training in anaesthesia.'),
('news-9th-conference','9th-sata-scientific-conference','9th SATA Scientific Conference','all','2025-05-29T09:00:00.000Z','SATA Secretariat','/images/news/conference-2025.jpg','{"label":"Conference photos","url":"https://photos.app.goo.gl/zGUJrtYq3Qgjxu5K7"}'::jsonb,'The 9th SATA Scientific Conference, themed **"Safe, Accessible, and Sustainable Anaesthesia for Children"**, took place from 7–9 May 2025 at Gold Crest Hotel, Mwanza. It brought together experts and professionals in paediatric anaesthesia to discuss advances, challenges, and best practice.

## Key takeaways

- Keynote addresses, presentations, and panel discussions on paediatric anaesthesia.
- Insights on paediatric patient blood management, cleft palate surgery, pain management, and regional anaesthesia.
- The role of point-of-care ultrasound (POCUS) in safe anaesthesia, and pharmacological updates.

## Panel discussions

- Educational programmes in paediatric anaesthesia
- Comprehensive cleft care
- Regional anaesthesia in paediatrics

## Outcomes

- Enhanced knowledge and practice in paediatric anaesthesia
- Improved understanding of safe and effective care for children undergoing surgery
- Opportunities for networking and collaboration among professionals

## Recommendations

- Continued education and training in paediatric anaesthesia
- Increased focus on resource-constrained settings
- Further research on regional anaesthesia in paediatrics'),
('news-aaac','aaac-2027-dar-es-salaam','AAAC 2027 is coming to Dar es Salaam','all','2026-10-15T09:00:00.000Z','SATA Secretariat','/images/aaac/hero-carousel-ChatGPT_Image_Jul_30__2026__07_20_59_PM.png','{"label":"Official AAAC 2027 website","url":"https://aaac2027.com"}'::jsonb,'SATA will host the **10th All Africa Anaesthesia Congress (AAAC 2027)** at the Julius Nyerere International Convention Centre (JNICC) in Dar es Salaam, **13–16 September 2027**, with pre-congress workshops on 12 September.

The theme is **The Future of Anaesthesia and Critical Care in Africa**, under the banner Smart · Safe · Inclusive.

Registration, abstract submission, sponsorship and travel information are published on the official congress website, aaac2027.com.'),
